d3b741bf05 Let a host recolour and hide OrcaSlicer's preview sliders

The G-code preview's layer and moves sliders paint their teal as an ImGui
literal that none of the existing colour tables reach. IMSlider gains two
neutral seams, both off by default:

- IMSlider::SetColorOverrides: a colour set for every slider. Each colour
  line falls back to its current built-in value while none is installed.
- IMSlider::show: whether one slider is drawn and takes wheel input. The
  wheel handler now needs only its own slider's window, since a hidden
  slider may never have created one.

apply_brand_palette installs the brand set from the tokens: the filled
track, the lower end dot and the value text in the action colour, each
handle a ring of it on the canvas colour, the unfilled track in the strong
border, the value boxes as raised surfaces with the subtle elevation.

